  "review_fixes": [
    "Serialize charging setters and multi-key behaviour reads; read CHLS before clearing inhibitors; expose both auto and auto-discharge for CHLS-only devices. Preserve persistent preference and CHWA behaviour.",
    "Own canonical GPU backing and both aliases before fallible initialization, ensuring aliases unmap before canonical storage on errors. This is defensive hardening, not a reproduced hardware crash.",
    "Track touching and palm IDs separately; forget latched palm state on a new landing; keep zero-area touching contacts; scope nonpositive-area rejection and bounded geometry to C1FE.",
    "Request contact-history reset on input reopen; consume the request only from the valid-report writer. Preserve non-J700 MTP/SPI numeric behaviour.",
    "Carry the additional PR151 pool-release observation/admission follow-up. Keep the existing firmware witness and physical identity lifetime; apply a 200ms retry budget outside both the mutex and preparation lease."
  ],
